# V1b: the single-card byte gate at FULL scope: selftest, every regime (R1 x5 seeds, R2, R3, R3b, RA, the 2,048-token R4 chain, R5 real text on layers 0, 23 and 47),
# users 1-3, the two negative controls, the stale-input sequence, 100 traced replays with the inputs restaged in place, the program-cache deltas, and the timing arms.
# Four users x 16 rows, K5-A against V5 bit for bit on raw page images. A full-scope PASS prints the sha256 triple (v5_triple) that gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED takes; commit
# it and build V3's image from that commit. The timing label (proceed at V - A <= -65 us, image-build at <= -40 us, kill otherwise; write-bound when V - V_nosnap >= 15 us) is
# informative: the byte verdict is the gate.
# Duration (estimate): 60-120 min (container timeout 3 h; the per-call watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only).
# Read: 'GDN_V5 verdict=PASS scope=full ...' and the last JSON line. STOP on FAIL or NO-DECISION; a FAIL with 'bytes>0' is a real difference.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/v5split window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/v5split and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are the driver's, on the
# allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is
# pushed from this branch.
# TWO IMAGES: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1 (a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes) is the build the single-card byte gate runs in (the gate mounts this
# checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs); C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-2 is the build of the commit that adds the
# qualified sha256 triple (gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED), which the four-card jobs serve. A reused tag is skipped by the build step.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/v5split/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1
